<details class="analysis screen-only"><summary>Course analysis guide · {{ shortTitle }}</summary>
<p>This is a course analysis diagram, not the artist’s historical process. Redraw by observation; use the guide to decide what to measure.</p>
{% if number == 6 %}<div class="branch-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Branch hierarchy: one trunk leads to three major limbs and then seven smaller limbs"><div>Trunk axis</div><div>Major limb 1 · Major limb 2 · Major limb 3</div><div>Smaller limbs → tapered twigs</div></div><p>Follow each branch from thick to thin. Change the fork angles and spacing; avoid a repeated pattern.</p>
{% elif number == 3 or number == 7 or number == 9 %}<div class="value-guide" role="img" aria-label="Three-value guide: light, middle, dark"><span>Light</span><span>Middle</span><span>Dark</span></div><p>Assign the largest shapes to these groups before choosing hatch marks. Paper can serve as the light.</p>
{% else %}<div class="construction-guide {% if number >= 11 and number <= 14 %}head-guide{% elif number >= 17 %}figure-guide{% endif %}" role="img" aria-label="Course construction guide: a bounding rectangle, central axis, and five anchor points{% if number >= 11 and number <= 14 %}, with an oval cranial envelope{% elif number >= 17 %}, with rib cage and pelvis masses{% endif %}"><span class="guide-axis"></span><i class="anchor top"></i><i class="anchor left"></i><i class="anchor center"></i><i class="anchor right"></i><i class="anchor bottom"></i><span class="guide-mass one"></span><span class="guide-mass two"></span></div><p>{% if number == 10 %}For an elevation, compare subdivisions across the centerline. For an oblique view, extend edges that are parallel in space toward a common vanishing point; separate different direction families.{% elif number >= 11 and number <= 14 %}Place the cranial envelope first. Tilt the face centerline and feature landmarks to match the observed head; these dots are measurement reminders, not universal facial proportions.{% elif number >= 17 %}Place rib cage and pelvis around the action line. Change their tilt and spacing to match the pose; use overlaps to connect the masses.{% else %}Choose your own highest, lowest, leftmost, and rightmost anchors. Adjust the central axis to the observed subject; check the envelope before refining the contour.{% endif %}</p>{% endif %}
</details>
